From 30901ec28c4a1c8c9bc93ecb5286aaecb553b144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:46:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fig. 2: labels inside the top-row schematics, tighter layout,
 16.8 x 8.5 cm

Labels (a)-(d) and the Herriott scale bar sit inside the schematics on
semi-transparent white boxes, so the top row loses its title lines. The
Herriott cells are drawn mirrored top to bottom (same simulation): port
at the bottom left, label at the top left. The CMPCs shrink to the
height of the two stacked Herriott views, which keep only a small gap.
The rows sit closer together and the bottom x-axis titles closer to
their tick labels. Default height 8.5 cm (21 cm preset: 10.4 cm).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NLfEqncaEw1RGMDLUGdFgb
